---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Getting started"
  description="Choose a desktop CLI, ESP32 detector or external receiver and follow the right AirHound setup guide."
>
  <header class="page-header wrap">
    <h1>Getting started</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Choose a desktop, firmware, or external receiver setup below. Each guide
      covers installation, permissions, and available output.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap content prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Check release status before installing.</strong>Hardware
      acceptance is incomplete for several paths.{" "}
      <a href="/downloads/">Downloads</a> distinguish published stable and
      preview releases; <a href="/hardware/">the receiver matrix</a> records
      limitations.
    </div>
    <h2 id="desktop">Desktop: macOS or Linux</h2>
    <p>
      The desktop component is a command-line scanner. The macOS app bundle
      supplies permission identity; it is not a graphical application.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <a href="/downloads/">Choose your operating system and architecture.</a>{" "}
        Preview package targets include Apple Silicon/macOS 15+ and Linux
        x86-64/glibc 2.35+. Other combinations require source builds.
      </li>
      <li>
        Follow{" "}
        <a href="/reference/hostd/">desktop installation and permissions</a>.
        macOS requires the appropriate Bluetooth and Location access; Linux
        requires its documented radio/system dependencies.
      </li>
      <li>
        Run the documented scan command, inspect observations, and choose NDJSON
        or WiGLE output.{" "}
        <a href="/reference/docs/desktop-scanner-health/">
          Scanner health guidance
        </a>{" "}
        explains startup and shutdown behavior.
      </li>
      <li>
        For receiver-location context, follow{" "}
        <a href="/reference/docs/gnss-wardriving/">gpsd setup</a>. A receiver
        fix is not the observed device’s location.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h2 id="firmware">ESP32 firmware: M5 or XIAO</h2>
    <p>
      Confirm the exact board before flashing. M5StickC Plus2 and XIAO ESP32-S3
      use different images; no_std and ESP-IDF are distinct runtime variants.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Read the <a href="/reference/docs/firmware/">firmware setup guide</a>{" "}
        and{" "}
        <a href="/reference/docs/release-status/">board acceptance status</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        For M5, follow{" "}
        <a href="/reference/docs/m5stickc-bringup/">
          backup and bring-up instructions
        </a>{" "}
        before replacing firmware. Select the correct board/runtime download.
      </li>
      <li>
        Check the display and{" "}
        <a href="/reference/docs/m5-controls/">buttons and sound controls</a>.
        Separate observed addresses from signature matches.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="small">
      A running detector’s observation stream is not yet a supported
      plug-and-play desktop ingestion source.{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/issues/175">
        Track that work in #175.
      </a>
    </p>
    <h2 id="external">External receivers</h2>
    <ul class="toc-list">
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/reference/docs/sniffle-source/">CatSniffer / Sniffle BLE</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Live passive capture and DLT256 replay. Install the upstream
          firmware/tools separately; start with the documented primary-channel
          limits.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/reference/drivers/mt7610u/">ALFA AWUS036ACHM / MT7610U</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Experimental userspace passive WiFi receiver, separately licensed and
          packaged. Read the endurance/RF limitations before use.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Observation output</h2>
    <p>
      Read{" "}
      <a href="/reference/docs/detection-evidence/">
        detection evidence and alert policy
      </a>{" "}
      before interpreting a match.{" "}
      <a href="/signatures/">Inspect the rule and its provenance</a>; a legacy
      label is not independent device validation.
    </p>
  </div>
</Site>
